1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,360
You can write K for any equation.

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:04,040
Now we put numbers in.

3
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:06,800
Almost every question
that asks you to calculate

4
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:09,440
with K is one of three types, and

5
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:11,920
what the question gives
you tells you which.

6
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:15,600
Type one gives you every
concentration at equilibrium,

7
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:18,120
so you substitute straight into K.

8
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,640
Type two gives you the start and just

9
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:23,280
one value at equilibrium, so you need a

10
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:25,120
table to find the rest first.

11
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,320
Type three gives you K and the start,

12
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:31,000
and asks for the concentrations
at equilibrium.

13
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:33,840
We'll take them easiest
first: types one and

14
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:36,000
two in this video, and type three in

15
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:36,640
the next.

16
00:00:37,867 --> 00:00:39,626
Type one is the quick one.

17
00:00:40,107 --> 00:00:42,346
Here is the hot hydrogen and iodine tube

18
00:00:42,427 --> 00:00:43,786
from earlier, settled.

19
00:00:44,347 --> 00:00:48,106
Each dot is 0.05 moles per litre, so

20
00:00:48,187 --> 00:00:51,946
it holds 0.10 moles per litre of hydrogen,

21
00:00:52,027 --> 00:00:56,586
0.10 of iodine and 0.70 of hydrogen

22
00:00:56,667 --> 00:00:57,546
iodide.

23
00:00:57,867 --> 00:01:01,786
Write the expression first:
hydrogen iodide squared, because

24
00:01:01,867 --> 00:01:05,706
its coefficient is two,
over hydrogen times iodine.

25
00:01:06,187 --> 00:01:11,466
Then substitute: 0.70 squared is 0.49,

26
00:01:11,547 --> 00:01:17,226
and 0.10 times 0.10 is 0.010,

27
00:01:17,307 --> 00:01:21,946
so K is 0.49 over 0.010, which

28
00:01:22,027 --> 00:01:23,146
is 49.

29
00:01:23,467 --> 00:01:25,546
If a type one question gives moles in

30
00:01:25,574 --> 00:01:28,506
a vessel, divide by
the volume first, because

31
00:01:28,587 --> 00:01:30,426
K uses concentrations.

32
00:01:31,634 --> 00:01:33,633
K belongs to the equation as it is

33
00:01:33,714 --> 00:01:34,113
written.

34
00:01:34,594 --> 00:01:39,873
Take the same settled tube, 0.10, 0.10 and

35
00:01:39,954 --> 00:01:44,353
0.70, and write the equation
backwards: two H

36
00:01:44,434 --> 00:01:47,113
I making hydrogen plus iodine.

37
00:01:47,394 --> 00:01:50,513
K is now hydrogen times iodine over H

38
00:01:50,594 --> 00:01:55,233
I squared: 0.10 times 0.10, over

39
00:01:55,314 --> 00:02:01,393
0.70 squared, is 0.010 over 0.49,

40
00:02:01,634 --> 00:02:06,593
about 0.020, and that is one over 49.

41
00:02:06,674 --> 00:02:08,913
Flip the equation, flip K.

42
00:02:09,154 --> 00:02:12,513
Double every coefficient
and every power doubles, so

43
00:02:12,594 --> 00:02:17,153
K is squared: 49 squared is 2401.

44
00:02:18,367 --> 00:02:20,846
Now type two, where the question gives you

45
00:02:20,927 --> 00:02:23,966
the start and just one
value at equilibrium,

46
00:02:24,087 --> 00:02:25,726
and you have to find K.

47
00:02:26,934 --> 00:02:28,773
Back to the PCl₅ flask

48
00:02:28,854 --> 00:02:29,493
from earlier.

49
00:02:30,054 --> 00:02:33,413
Suppose we seal 0.40 moles of

50
00:02:33,494 --> 00:02:36,453
PCl₅ into a 2.0 litre flask and

51
00:02:36,534 --> 00:02:39,013
heat it, and this time we measure just

52
00:02:39,174 --> 00:02:40,173
one thing.

53
00:02:40,614 --> 00:02:43,493
Chlorine is yellow-green,
so its colour tells us

54
00:02:43,574 --> 00:02:46,213
how much is there, and at equilibrium it

55
00:02:46,374 --> 00:02:49,733
reads 0.080 moles per litre.

56
00:02:50,534 --> 00:02:52,693
Can we work out the other
two concentrations

57
00:02:52,774 --> 00:02:55,253
from it, and then
the equilibrium constant?

58
00:02:56,467 --> 00:02:59,186
To keep track of every
concentration, we use

59
00:02:59,307 --> 00:03:02,706
an ICE table: I for initial,

60
00:03:02,787 --> 00:03:05,506
C for change, and E for equilibrium.

61
00:03:06,067 --> 00:03:08,146
It has a column for each substance and

62
00:03:08,227 --> 00:03:10,706
a row for each of those three stages.

63
00:03:11,027 --> 00:03:13,146
We fill the initial row first.

64
00:03:13,507 --> 00:03:17,826
K uses concentrations,
not moles, so divide: 0.40

65
00:03:17,987 --> 00:03:22,706
moles over 2.0 litres is 0.20

66
00:03:22,867 --> 00:03:25,266
moles per litre of PCl₅,

67
00:03:25,347 --> 00:03:27,426
and the two products start at zero.

68
00:03:28,634 --> 00:03:30,873
Next, the one value we measured.

69
00:03:31,434 --> 00:03:36,633
Chlorine is 0.080 moles
per litre at equilibrium,

70
00:03:36,714 --> 00:03:39,113
so it goes straight into
the equilibrium row,

71
00:03:39,234 --> 00:03:40,233
under chlorine.

72
00:03:40,554 --> 00:03:42,633
Now the table gives us its change.

73
00:03:43,114 --> 00:03:46,953
Change is equilibrium minus
initial, because the change

74
00:03:47,034 --> 00:03:49,353
is how far it moved from the start:

75
00:03:49,434 --> 00:03:55,593
0.080 minus zero is plus 0.080.

76
00:03:55,674 --> 00:03:57,673
That is always the first move in a

77
00:03:57,794 --> 00:04:00,393
type two question:
the measured value goes in

78
00:04:00,434 --> 00:04:03,513
the equilibrium row,
then subtract to find its

79
00:04:03,594 --> 00:04:04,233
change.

80
00:04:05,434 --> 00:04:07,233
How much did the others change?

81
00:04:07,514 --> 00:04:09,993
Each PCl₅ that splits makes

82
00:04:10,154 --> 00:04:13,033
one PCl₃ and one chlorine.

83
00:04:13,354 --> 00:04:15,833
So PCl₃ also rises by

84
00:04:15,994 --> 00:04:20,233
0.080, and PCl₅ falls by

85
00:04:20,314 --> 00:04:24,073
0.080, because one is used up for every

86
00:04:24,154 --> 00:04:25,313
chlorine made.

87
00:04:25,594 --> 00:04:27,833
The change row follows
the coefficients in the

88
00:04:27,954 --> 00:04:28,753
equation.

89
00:04:29,034 --> 00:04:31,513
A substance used up gets a minus sign

90
00:04:31,754 --> 00:04:34,073
and a substance made gets a plus.

91
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:37,540
Now complete the equilibrium row.

92
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:40,100
Each box is the initial value plus the

93
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:41,020
change.

94
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:45,700
PCl₅: 0.20 plus the change,

95
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:50,260
minus 0.080, is 0.12.

96
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:55,220
PCl₃: zero plus 0.080 is

97
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:57,300
0.080.

98
00:04:57,340 --> 00:05:00,580
Chlorine is already
filled in, and it agrees:

99
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:05,300
zero plus 0.080 is 0.080.

100
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:07,100
Now K.

101
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:11,380
Products over reactants,
with every coefficient one: K

102
00:05:11,540 --> 00:05:14,500
equals PCl₃ times chlorine, over

103
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:16,020
PCl₅.

104
00:05:16,260 --> 00:05:21,060
Substitute the equilibrium
values: 0.080 times

105
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:24,820
0.080, over 0.12.

106
00:05:25,060 --> 00:05:30,980
The top is 0.0064, and 0.0064 divided

107
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:35,620
by 0.12 is 0.0533,

108
00:05:35,740 --> 00:05:40,060
so K is 0.053 to two significant figures.

109
00:05:40,260 --> 00:05:45,380
Check the subtraction: 0.12 plus 0.080 is

110
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:48,100
0.20, what we started with.

111
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:51,740
Two habits make type two work.

112
00:05:52,020 --> 00:05:55,060
First, the measured value
goes in the equilibrium

113
00:05:55,140 --> 00:05:57,860
row, and its change comes from the table.

114
00:05:58,180 --> 00:06:02,020
Second, only the change row
follows the coefficients:

115
00:06:02,180 --> 00:06:07,060
minus 0.080, plus 0.080 and

116
00:06:07,260 --> 00:06:11,420
plus 0.080 are one to one to one.

117
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:13,700
The equilibrium row does not have to be

118
00:06:13,780 --> 00:06:18,500
in that ratio: 0.12, 0.080 and

119
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:20,820
0.080 are not.

120
00:06:22,034 --> 00:06:22,673
Your turn.

121
00:06:23,234 --> 00:06:27,393
Dinitrogen tetroxide, N₂O₄, splits into

122
00:06:27,474 --> 00:06:29,793
nitrogen dioxide, NO₂.

123
00:06:30,354 --> 00:06:34,033
We seal 0.100 moles of

124
00:06:34,114 --> 00:06:37,633
N₂O₄, and nothing else, in a 2.00 litre

125
00:06:37,714 --> 00:06:40,833
vessel at a steady temperature,
and at equilibrium

126
00:06:41,074 --> 00:06:45,393
the concentration of NO₂ is 0.0300

127
00:06:45,554 --> 00:06:47,233
moles per litre.

128
00:06:47,394 --> 00:06:49,953
One: find K for N₂O₄

129
00:06:50,194 --> 00:06:52,433
making two NO₂.

130
00:06:52,594 --> 00:06:54,993
Two: what is K for the equation written

131
00:06:55,074 --> 00:06:57,713
the other way, two NO₂ making

132
00:06:57,874 --> 00:07:00,113
N₂O₄, at the same temperature?

133
00:07:00,594 --> 00:07:01,873
Pause here to answer.

134
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:12,940
One.

135
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:17,900
Start with concentrations:
0.100 moles over

136
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:22,780
2.00 litres is 0.0500 moles

137
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:25,340
per litre of N₂O₄, and

138
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:27,380
NO₂ starts at zero.

139
00:07:27,740 --> 00:07:32,060
The measured 0.0300 goes
in the equilibrium row

140
00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:35,020
first, under NO₂, so its change

141
00:07:35,100 --> 00:07:41,740
is 0.0300 minus zero, plus 0.0300.

142
00:07:41,780 --> 00:07:43,980
The equation makes two NO₂ for

143
00:07:44,060 --> 00:07:46,140
each N₂O₄, so

144
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:50,700
N₂O₄ fell by half of that, 0.0150.

145
00:07:50,780 --> 00:07:55,580
Equilibrium N₂O₄ is 0.0500 minus

146
00:07:55,740 --> 00:08:00,860
0.0150, 0.0350.

147
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:03,180
K is NO₂ squared over

148
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:10,940
N₂O₄: 0.0300 squared is 0.000900,

149
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:16,460
over 0.0350, gives 0.0257.

150
00:08:17,667 --> 00:08:21,266
If you got about 0.018, you used the

151
00:08:21,547 --> 00:08:28,146
starting 0.0500 instead
of the equilibrium 0.0350.

152
00:08:28,227 --> 00:08:31,506
If you got 0.045, you took off the

153
00:08:31,587 --> 00:08:35,506
whole 0.0300 instead of half of it.

154
00:08:35,667 --> 00:08:38,706
And if you got about 0.86, you forgot

155
00:08:38,787 --> 00:08:40,226
to square the NO₂.

156
00:08:41,434 --> 00:08:41,833
Two.

157
00:08:42,114 --> 00:08:45,833
Written backwards,
K is the old value flipped,

158
00:08:45,914 --> 00:08:49,913
so it is one over 0.0257, which is

159
00:08:50,074 --> 00:08:51,753
38.9.

160
00:08:51,834 --> 00:08:54,473
The expression is N₂O₄ over

161
00:08:54,554 --> 00:08:56,313
NO₂ squared.

162
00:08:56,394 --> 00:09:00,473
If you wrote 0.0257 again,
check the direction

163
00:09:00,514 --> 00:09:03,073
of the equation: the products are now the

164
00:09:03,194 --> 00:09:04,313
N₂O₄.

165
00:09:05,534 --> 00:09:09,213
So, for type one, every
equilibrium concentration is

166
00:09:09,294 --> 00:09:12,373
given: write the expression
and substitute.

167
00:09:12,654 --> 00:09:14,973
For type two, you get the start and

168
00:09:15,134 --> 00:09:16,573
one equilibrium value.

169
00:09:17,054 --> 00:09:18,893
Put the start in the initial row and

170
00:09:18,974 --> 00:09:22,013
the measured value in the
equilibrium row, subtract

171
00:09:22,054 --> 00:09:24,573
to get its change,
use the coefficients for

172
00:09:24,614 --> 00:09:27,693
the other changes, then
complete the equilibrium row

173
00:09:27,854 --> 00:09:28,733
and substitute.

174
00:09:29,294 --> 00:09:32,293
If the equation is written
backwards, flip K.

175
00:09:32,734 --> 00:09:35,613
Next: type three, where you know K and

176
00:09:35,694 --> 00:09:37,453
have to find the concentrations.

177
00:09:38,667 --> 00:09:40,106
Here are the key notes.

178
00:09:40,347 --> 00:09:42,266
Pause the video if you need more time

179
00:09:42,347 --> 00:09:43,146
to copy them.
